  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/... \nBenign weather conditions will continue well into next week with the \nlingering trough finally moving out of the region and being replaced \nby weak ridging to zonal westerly flow. This pattern shift will \nmaintain mostly clear skies and dry conditions, while allowing \ntemperatures to gradually warm back into a near normal range through \nat least the first half of next week. Expect the bulk of the lower \ndeserts to have daily highs in the lower to middle 80s and lows from \nthe mid 50s to mid 60s during the first half of next week. Model \nuncertainty grows later next week as there are hints at some \nmoisture return into the region from the southeast, then a potential \natmospheric river approaching by next weekend. Either, or both of \nthese moisture sources may eventually help to bring a return to rain \nchances at some point before the end of the month, but it is too \nearly to have a good idea on timing and/or placement for any weather \nfeature this far in advance.",
